export const WITNESS_HTML = "<p><strong>Case ID:</strong> {{CASE_ID}}  \u00b7  <strong>Date:</strong> {{DATE}}</p>\n<p>This form is between:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>You:</strong> {{SIGNER}} (\"you\")</li>\n<li><strong>FoxLock Security</strong> (\"we\", \"FoxLock\")</li>\n</ul>\n<p>FoxLock is helping our client, {{CLIENT}}, document harassing messages that were sent about her to people she knows. You may have received some of those messages. This form explains what we would like from you, what we will do with it, and what we will never do. <strong>Taking part is completely voluntary.</strong> You can say no, cross out anything below, or withdraw at any time (section 7).</p>\n<p>You are not our client, and you are not being investigated. We are only interested in what was sent to you.</p>\n<h2>1. What you agree to share</h2>\n<p>Tick what you are comfortable with:</p>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"choice\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"share_messages\" value=\"yes\"> <span><strong>Copies of the messages</strong> you received about {{CLIENT}} or from the sender's accounts (emails, texts, DMs), as original files (.eml) and/or screenshots.</span></label></li>\n<li class=\"choice\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"share_alerts\" value=\"yes\"> <span><strong>Security alerts</strong> you received around the same time (for example login alerts or password reset emails), with any codes covered.</span></label></li>\n<li class=\"choice\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"share_statement\" value=\"yes\"> <span><strong>A short written statement</strong> from you: when you received the messages and anything else you noticed.</span></label></li>\n<li class=\"choice\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"share_contact\" value=\"yes\"> <span><strong>Your email address and/or username</strong>, used only to work out how the sender may have found you (for example, from public profiles or old contact lists).</span></label></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2. Optional: a check of your own account security</h2>\n<p>If you received an unexpected login alert, we can go through your account's security with you. <strong>You</strong> sign in on your own device and type your own password; we look at sign-in history, connected apps, recovery details and forwarding settings together, and suggest fixes for you to make.</p>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"choice\"><label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"account_check\" value=\"yes\"> <span>Yes, I'd like this check for: <input type=\"text\" name=\"account_check_for\" maxlength=\"80\" placeholder=\"which account\"> (e.g. X/Twitter, Gmail)</span></label></li>\n<li class=\"choice\"><label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"account_check\" value=\"no\"> <span>No thanks</span></label></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>3. How your information is used</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Only to document the harassment of {{CLIENT}}: an evidence package for platform abuse reports, police, a court (for example a restraining order), and any lawyer {{CLIENT}} works with.</li>\n<li>Each file you give us is kept unchanged, with a fingerprint (a SHA-256 hash) so anyone can later check it was not altered.</li>\n<li><strong>Your name in the package</strong> (choose one):</li>\n<li class=\"choice\"><label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"name_in_packet\" value=\"name\"> <span>My name can appear in the evidence package.</span></label></li>\n<li class=\"choice\"><label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"name_in_packet\" value=\"label\"> <span>Please refer to me by a label (e.g. \"Witness A\"). My name is shared only if police or a court require it.</span></label></li>\n<li>You may be asked by police or a court to confirm what you received. Whether you take part is up to you.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4. What we will not do</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>We will never ask for your passwords, login codes or recovery codes.</li>\n<li>We will not sign in to, or look through, any of your accounts or devices. Only what you choose to hand us is used.</li>\n<li>We will not read or keep anything else from your inbox or phone, and we will not look into your personal life.</li>\n<li>We will not share what you give us with anyone except as described in section 3, and never publish it.</li>\n<li>We will not contact the sender, or tell him you helped.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>5. Storage and deletion</h2>\n<p>Your files are kept in encrypted storage that only the people working on this case can access. They are kept for <strong>90 days</strong> after the case report is delivered, unless they are needed longer for a police or court case, and then deleted. You can ask us at any time what we hold from you.</p>\n<h2>6. Be safe</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Don't reply to or forward the sender's messages, and don't delete them.</li>\n<li>If you ever feel unsafe, call 911. FoxLock is not law enforcement and not a law firm, and this form is not legal advice.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>7. Withdrawal</h2>\n<p>You can withdraw at any time by text or in writing. We will stop using your files and delete them. Anything already given to police or a court before you withdrew stays with them, but we will tell you exactly what was shared.</p>";
